---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import KuraMosaic from '../components/KuraMosaic.astro';
import LoadingDiagram from '../components/LoadingDiagram.astro';
import PipelineDiagram from '../components/PipelineDiagram.astro';
import KuraDiagram from '../components/KuraDiagram.astro';
import Playbooks from '../components/Playbooks.astro';
import SizeLadder from '../components/SizeLadder.astro';
import ProfileLanes from '../components/ProfileLanes.astro';
import Terminal from '../components/Terminal.astro';
import { bundles, sources, stats } from '../lib/catalog';
import { links } from '../lib/site';
import { caseCount } from '../lib/usecases';

const topSources = sources.slice(0, 8);
const remainingSources = sources.length - topSources.length;
const seats = bundles.filter((bundle) => bundle.agents.some((agent) => agent.endsWith('-staff-engineer')));
const productTeam = bundles.find((bundle) => bundle.name === 'product-team');
---

<Base
  dark
  title="Agent Catalog: skills, agents and bundles for Claude Code and Pi"
  description={`${stats.skills} skills, ${stats.agents} agents and ${stats.bundles} bundles that teach your coding agent how your team works, installed per project with kura.`}
>
  <section class="hero" data-hero>
    <KuraMosaic />
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>Teach your coding agent how your team works.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          {stats.skills} skills and {stats.agents} specialist agents that give your agent judgment, checklists, and the habit of
          asking before it does something you would have stopped. kura puts the right ones in each project.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="/docs/start/">Set it up in ten minutes</a>
          <a class="button ghost" href="#what">See how a skill works</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="glyph-slot" data-glyph-slot aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap hero-foot">
      <p class="hint">蔵 means storehouse. Every gold or indigo tile is one skill; hover to read its label.</p>
      <ul class="legend">
        <li><i class="local"></i>{stats.local} written here</li>
        <li><i class="upstream"></i>{stats.upstream} from {stats.sources} open-source repos</li>
        <li><i class="spare"></i>stone, no skill yet</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section id="problem" question="What goes wrong without it?">
    <p class="lede">
      A coding agent takes the shortest path that looks finished. Ask both of these for the same thing and watch where they
      stop.
    </p>
    <div class="duel">
      <figure class="session plain">
        <figcaption>Your agent, on its own</figcaption>
        <div class="screen">
          <p class="you">&gt; Add a newsletter signup form to the footer</p>
          <p>Installing react-hook-form and zod…</p>
          <p class="flag">Created NewsletterForm.tsx<span class="note">You replaced that library last year.</span></p>
          <p class="flag">Styled the button with #3b82f6<span class="note">Not your blue. Yours is a token.</span></p>
          <p class="flag">Wired submit to POST /api/subscribe<span class="note">Nothing stops a second click.</span></p>
          <p class="flag">Done. All tests pass ✓<span class="note">There were no tests for this.</span></p>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="session catalog">
        <figcaption>Your agent, with the catalog</figcaption>
        <div class="screen">
          <p class="you">&gt; Add a newsletter signup form to the footer</p>
          <p class="seat">frontend-staff-engineer</p>
          <p>Stack: React 19, forms through <span class="ok">ui/form</span></p>
          <p>Opened: forms-and-input, accessibility, errors-and-resilience</p>
          <p><span class="ok">✓</span> Double submit guarded, re-enabled on failure</p>
          <p><span class="ok">✓</span> Errors announced, labels tied to inputs</p>
          <p><span class="ask">needs-decision</span> Add an email validator, or reuse ui/form? Recommend: reuse.</p>
          <p class="report">Status: needs-decision, one question for you</p>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p>
      The model is the one you already use. The difference is that it reads instructions written by people who have shipped
      this kind of change before, at the moment they matter.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="what" question="What is a skill, and how does it stay out of the way?" tone="deep">
    <p class="lede">
      A skill is a folder with a Markdown file in it. The first lines say when to use it. The rest says how. Your agent reads
      the first part always and the rest only when your task calls for it.
    </p>
    <LoadingDiagram />
  </Section>

  <Section id="parts" question="Skills, agents, bundles: which one do I need?">
    <Fragment slot="aside">
      <p>Pick a size to see the jobs that need it, with the exact commands.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <p class="lede">
      The size of the job decides. Most work needs one skill; a whole pipeline is for the few changes that cross layers.
    </p>
    <SizeLadder />
    <p>
      All of it runs inside your harness, the program that runs the model: Claude Code or Pi. Skills are plain Markdown, so
      the knowledge travels, and kura handles the wiring for each. <a href="/docs/concepts/">Read the concepts page</a> for
      the anatomy of each, with real files.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="who" question="Who uses it, and where do they come in?" tone="deep">
    <Fragment slot="aside">
      <p>Gold cells are gates: a person decides there, and nothing moves on until they do.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <p class="lede">
      Product managers shape the work, engineers build it, and stakeholders decide at the gates. Each one reaches for a
      different part of the catalog.
    </p>
    <ProfileLanes />
  </Section>

  <Section id="seats" question="Who is on the team?" tone="dark">
    <Fragment slot="aside">
      <p>Add a seat with <code>kura add frontend --type bundle</code>. Each one arrives with the checklist it is held to.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <p class="lede">
      Sixteen staff-engineer seats, one per discipline. Your agent hands each one the slice it owns; the seat clears its own
      failure-modes checklist before it may report done.
    </p>
    <ol class="chart">
      {
        seats.map((bundle) => (
          <li>
            <h3>
              <a href={`/team/#seat-${bundle.name}`}>{bundle.name}</a>
            </h3>
            <p>{bundle.job}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
    <p class="more">
      <a href="/team/">Meet the whole team</a>: which seat to pick for a job, which to pick instead, and the agents that route
      work to them.
    </p>
    {
      productTeam && (
        <p class="pm">
          Plus <strong>product-team</strong>: {productTeam.agents.length} agents and {productTeam.skills.length} skills that take a
          raw idea through research, a PRD and a red team before any engineer is involved.
        </p>
      )
    }
  </Section>

  <Section id="flow" question="How does a request turn into a reviewed pull request?">
    <p class="lede">
      For work bigger than one file, the catalog runs a pipeline. Agents do the reading, writing and checking. You stand at
      the two gates where a wrong call is expensive.
    </p>
    <PipelineDiagram />
    <p><a href="/docs/workflow/">The full workflow</a>, including the product pipeline that comes before it.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="playbooks" question="What does this look like on a real project?" tone="deep">
    <Fragment slot="aside">
      <p>Pick the situation closest to yours. Each one is the commands you type and what runs because of them.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <Playbooks />
    <p class="more">
      <a href="/docs/playbooks/">All playbooks, with the reasoning behind each step</a>, or <a href="/docs/use-cases/">browse {caseCount} use cases by size</a>.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="kura" question="Why kura?" tone="dark">
    <p class="lede">
      Copying skill folders by hand works for three skills. At three hundred, across several projects and two harnesses, you
      need something that knows what each repository is supposed to see. kura (蔵, a storehouse) is that something.
    </p>
    <KuraDiagram />
    <ul class="reasons">
      <li><strong>One source of truth.</strong> Skills live once, in the catalog. Projects get links, never copies, so a fix lands everywhere.</li>
      <li><strong>Per-project intent.</strong> A <code>kura.json</code> at the repo root says what this project uses. Commit it and your team gets the same setup.</li>
      <li><strong>Evidence, not guesses.</strong> <code>kura scout</code> reads your manifests and recommends skills with the line that justifies each one.</li>
      <li><strong>Drift is visible.</strong> <code>kura doctor</code> reports broken links, missing skills and untrusted projects before your agent trips on them.</li>
      <li><strong>Upstream stays fresh.</strong> <code>kura outdated</code> and <code>kura update</code> pull new versions from each source repo at a pinned commit.</li>
    </ul>
    <Terminal
      label="A first kura session"
      lines={[
        { kind: 'comment', text: '# in any project' },
        { text: 'kura init --harness claude --harness pi --yes' },
        { text: 'kura scout' },
        { kind: 'out', text: 'Strong match' },
        { kind: 'out', text: '  · react-router (skill) [engineering, frontend, react-router]' },
        { kind: 'out', text: '    Why:  react-router in package.json' },
        { kind: 'out', text: '  · frontend (bundle) [engineering, frontend, observability]' },
        { kind: 'out', text: '    Adds: frontend-staff-engineer (agent), frontend-failure-modes' },
        { text: 'kura scout --add' },
        { text: 'kura trust --on' },
        { text: 'kura doctor' },
      ]}
    />
    <p class="more"><a href="/docs/kura/">The kura guide</a> covers every command and when to reach for it.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="fit" question="Is it worth it for me?">
    <div class="ledger">
      <div>
        <h3>Where it earns its keep</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>You work in one codebase long enough for its conventions to matter.</li>
          <li>Changes cross layers, and you want each layer checked by something that knows it.</li>
          <li>You would rather be asked than surprised: dependencies, breaking APIs, new design tokens.</li>
          <li>You want the same agent behavior on every machine and for every teammate.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Where it costs more than it gives</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>One-off scripts and quick questions. The full pipeline is a tax on a two-line fix; use one seat or none.</li>
          <li>Token budgets. Seats default to the strongest model at high effort, and a feature team runs several of them.</li>
          <li>Full autonomy. Every gate is a person by design, and no agent commits, pushes or merges.</li>
          <li>Harnesses other than Claude Code and Pi. The Markdown travels, but kura only wires those two.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      One more honest number: {sources[0]?.skills.length} of the {stats.upstream} upstream skills come from a single source, {sources[0]?.repo},
      and most of them cover Google Cloud. If you do not use it, you will not install them, but they do inflate the total.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="credit" question="Who wrote all of this?" tone="deep">
    <p class="lede">
      {stats.local} skills and every agent were written for this catalog. The other {stats.upstream} skills come from {stats.sources}
      open-source repositories, kept as they were published and credited by name.
    </p>
    <ol class="sources">
      {
        topSources.map((source) => (
          <li>
            <span class="count">{source.skills.length}</span>
            <code>{source.repo}</code>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
    <p>
      and {remainingSources} more. Each upstream skill is pinned to the exact commit it was copied from, keeps its license, and
      is listed on the <a href="/attribution/">attribution page</a> with a link back to its source.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="start" question="How do I get the most out of it?">
    <ol class="climb">
      <li>
        <h3>Install the global layer</h3>
        <p>Clone the catalog, point kura at it, run <code>kura sync</code>. Every repository on your machine now has triage, commit, ship, review and the teammate skills.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Let scout pick the project layer</h3>
        <p><code>kura init</code> then <code>kura scout --add</code> in each project. Commit <code>kura.json</code> so your team gets the same set.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Add the seats your work touches</h3>
        <p><code>kura add frontend backend qa --type bundle</code>. A seat is worth adding when you would want a specialist reviewing that layer.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Write your decisions down</h3>
        <p>ADRs and recorded rulings are what let <code>decision-judge</code> answer instead of asking. The second month is quieter than the first.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Route work instead of prompting it</h3>
        <p>Start from <code>/triage</code> or <code>/feature-team</code> rather than a blank prompt, and end with <code>/ship</code>.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Keep it fresh</h3>
        <p><code>kura outdated</code> once a week, <code>kura doctor</code> when something feels off, and the <code>watch</code> skill to sweep for dead code and stale workarounds.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/docs/start/">Start the setup guide</a>
      <a class="button" href={links.catalog}>Open the repository</a>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    background: #1b2226;
    color: var(--grout);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    background:
      linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(27, 34, 38, 0.94) 0%, rgba(27, 34, 38, 0.82) 34%, rgba(27, 34, 38, 0) 58%),
      linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(27, 34, 38, 0.9) 0%, rgba(27, 34, 38, 0) 22%);
  }

  .hero-grid,
  .hero-foot {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    align-items: center;
    min-height: min(calc(100svh - 9rem), 58rem);
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem) 1rem;
  }

  .hero-copy {
    pointer-events: auto;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 6.4vw, 6.25rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    max-width: 11ch;
    color: var(--grout);
  }

  .hero .lede {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    max-width: 34rem;
    color: #c7cfcb;
  }

  .glyph-slot {
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    width: 100%;
    max-height: min(72svh, 44rem);
    justify-self: end;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
  }

  .button.ghost {
    color: var(--grout);
    border-color: #6b7a82;
  }

  .button.ghost:hover {
    background: var(--grout);
    border-color: var(--grout);
    color: var(--sumi);
  }

  .hero-foot {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.75rem 2rem;
    padding-block: 1.5rem 2.25rem;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: #9fabb0;
  }

  .hint {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.25rem;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .legend i {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.7em;
    height: 0.7em;
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    margin-right: 0.5em;
  }

  .legend .local {
    background: #5b80cf;
  }

  .legend .upstream {
    background: #d6a447;
  }

  .legend .spare {
    background: #7f8c91;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .hero::after {
      background: linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(27, 34, 38, 0.96) 0%, rgba(27, 34, 38, 0.85) 50%, rgba(27, 34, 38, 0.1) 75%);
    }

    .hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      min-height: 0;
    }

    .glyph-slot {
      order: -1;
      width: min(100%, 26rem);
      justify-self: center;
    }
  }

  .duel {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-block: 2rem;
  }

  .session {
    margin: 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius-panel);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--slate-deep);
    color: #dde2de;
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .session figcaption {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem;
    background: #2f3a40;
  }

  .catalog figcaption {
    background: var(--ai);
  }

  .screen {
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem 1.25rem;
  }

  .screen p {
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
  }

  .you {
    color: #e2c47f;
  }

  .flag {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 0.8rem;
    border-left: 2px solid #c2604a;
  }

  .flag .note {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: #f0a796;
  }

  .seat {
    color: #a9bfe6;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .ok {
    color: #9fd3a8;
  }

  .ask {
    color: #1e2124;
    background: #e2c47f;
    padding: 0 0.35em;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  .report {
    margin-top: 0.8rem !important;
    padding-top: 0.6rem;
    border-top: 1px dashed #4a5860;
    color: #e2c47f;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .duel {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .chart {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 1.5rem;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(13rem, 1fr));
    border-top: 1px solid #34404a;
    border-left: 1px solid #34404a;
  }

  .chart li {
    padding: 1.1rem 1.15rem 1.2rem;
    border-right: 1px solid #34404a;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #34404a;
    transition: background-color 160ms ease-out;
  }

  .chart li:hover {
    background: #232c31;
  }

  .chart h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--grout);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .chart h3::before {
    content: '';
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.32em;
    height: 0.32em;
    background: var(--ochre);
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    margin-right: 0.45em;
    vertical-align: 0.2em;
  }

  .chart p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: #a7b2b6;
  }

  .chart h3 a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .chart h3 a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .pm {
    color: #c7cfcb;
  }

  .pm strong {
    color: var(--grout);
  }
  .more {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  .reasons {
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }

  .reasons li {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .reasons li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.15rem;
    top: 0.6em;
    width: 0.5em;
    height: 0.5em;
    background: var(--ochre);
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }

  .ledger ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }

  .ledger li + li {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
  }

  .ledger {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .ledger h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.6rem;
    border-bottom: 3px solid var(--ai);
  }

  .ledger > div + div h3 {
    border-color: var(--ochre);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .ledger {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .sources {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 2rem 0 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
    gap: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .sources li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .count {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    color: var(--ochre-ink);
    min-width: 2.2ch;
    text-align: right;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .sources code {
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .climb {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: climb;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }

  .climb li {
    counter-increment: climb;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    column-gap: 1rem;
  }

  .climb li::before {
    content: counter(climb);
    grid-row: span 2;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--ai);
  }

  .climb h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .climb p {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
